    "acceptance": "Shared objects: empty-root, installed and removed-root runtime sessions; automatic discovery uses the production registered sidecar, retained source, correct relocated function, prototype/type/argument values and source stepping. Sectionless: independent compiler controls prove the tested GDB cannot discover matching full DWARF without original section headers; original shoff/shnum/shstrndx are independently zero-checked. Installed automatic discovery remains absent, while explicitly loading the installed sidecar proves source lookup, exact reference address, breakpoint, stepping and normal exit. No symbol-file is used in shared-object automatic tests.",
    "consumerLimitation": "GDB 15.1 does not automatically discover either Forge or matching compiler debug files for these sectionless ET_EXEC inputs. Installation and retained source validate, but this is not automatic-discovery acceptance. The helper now reports this limitation and explicit-loading alternatives on install/update.",
    "diagnostics": "ARM32/AArch64 QEMU system-supplied DSO corrupt-string-table-index warning is present identically with an empty debug root and no Forge symbols. The oracle accepts only that exact diagnostic shape, requires equality with the negative baseline, retains it, and rejects other diagnostics. It is not a Forge DWARF validator warning.",
    "historicalTrials": [
        "ARM fixture build initially lacked the isolated toolchain shared-library path; adding its local LD_LIBRARY_PATH and explicit strip/objcopy paths completed the build.",
        "Initial sectionless automatic tests failed as recorded; matching compiler controls confirmed consumer limitation, then explicit fallback was tested separately.",
        "Initial ARM oracle omitted the independently observed system-DSO baseline warning.",
        "Initial MIPS sectionless oracle assumed FUN_<main-address>; Ghidra actually preserves main. Final oracle admits either known name and still requires the exact compiler-reference address and selected sidecar/source."
    ],
